level2-v12.bin
--------------

TRS-80 Model I Level II BASIC, version 1.2. Written by Microsoft for
Tandy Corporation (Radio Shack). It boots with "MEMORY SIZE?" and
"RADIO SHACK LEVEL II BASIC".

  Size     12288 bytes
  SHA-256  3cd3824d2ac2743750d2179951ed812794302b885ccb4f98aa2579b352c4b00e
  Load     absolute at 0000H (0000H-2FFFH)

It is the Model I's two ROMs joined as the computer sees them: ROM A
(Z33, 8 KB at 0000H) and the used half of ROM B (Z34, 4 KB at 2000H).
tools/vendor.mjs makes it from src/rom_a_L2_v12.bin and
src/rom_b_L2_v12.bin, taken from RetroStack's ROM repository at a
pinned commit and checked by their SHA-256:

  https://github.com/RetroStack/TRS-80-Model-I-System-ROMs
  (commit 3f31faebde2214214acb74f87f06b836df3914d2, 1-Option_2x64/)

  src/rom_a_L2_v12.bin  SHA-256 3d07912ff154dbf0174c25691fd1e4502ff6c15292202c8193a6ae89636b7fc5
  src/rom_b_L2_v12.bin  SHA-256 a59d730f3ef732119f354bb571314e4530b9f707dba231a28fa89aacb57c3295

The joined image is identical, byte for byte, to model1-level2.rom in
Lawrence Kesteloot's TRS-80 emulator, an independent second copy:

  https://github.com/lkesteloot/trs80  (packages/trs80-emulator/roms/)

The copyright in this program is Microsoft's and Tandy's. It has never
been formally released, and no licence to redistribute it has been
granted. It is included here on the same footing as the other open
TRS-80 emulators and preservation archives that carry it: as a
